#pragma rhoform-syntax 0.2

# A 0.2 file may bind `supply`; 0.3 reserves it (RHO1019). So the RHO1016
# its `warning` draws cannot promise that 0.3 only adds: its fix-it is
# needs-review, and its message names the word to rename.
module Rail:
    port vin power_in
    supply = new rhoform.lib.passive.Resistor(resistance = 1kohm)
    supply.a ~ vin
    net SUPPLY:
        supply.b
    assert rail static operating_point(SUPPLY) at most 5.5V warning
